1
00:27:35,746 --> 00:27:36,769
Where is it?

2
00:27:37,089 --> 00:27:39,667
I think the little
darling is in that closet.

3
00:27:42,148 --> 00:27:45,073
You know, it's a pity you
leased this house Miss Van Gorder.

4
00:27:45,103 --> 00:27:46,020
Why a pity?

5
00:27:46,736 --> 00:27:48,917
Well, my dear lady, I don't
want to alarm you but...

6
00:27:49,033 --> 00:27:51,968
Oh, after tonight nothing can alarm me.

7
00:27:52,113 --> 00:27:54,671
Yes, I understand,
it must've been terrifying.

8
00:27:55,550 --> 00:27:58,736
So many unexplainable
things had happened here.

9
00:27:59,325 --> 00:28:00,948
It's something about the place.

10
00:28:01,836 --> 00:28:05,457
Your servants must've sensed it
when they walked out on you...

11
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:08,238
an apprehension of disaster.

12
00:28:09,290 --> 00:28:10,971
Well, let's see.

13
00:28:13,395 --> 00:28:15,394
Yes, there he is.

14
00:28:15,424 --> 00:28:21,343
All right now, take it easy, nobody is
going to hurt you, quiet now, quiet.

15
00:28:27,277 --> 00:28:30,009
Looks quite normal,
doesn't seem to be sick at all.

16
00:28:30,850 --> 00:28:34,269
Ain't that nice. I've
been worried about him.

17
00:28:34,761 --> 00:28:36,122
Well, you should be.

18
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:40,834
From his appearance, I'd say
that he doesn't have any infection.

19
00:28:41,973 --> 00:28:44,773
In which case, you had a narrow escape.

20
00:28:46,839 --> 00:28:50,711
Now, you take one of those tablets I left
for you and I'll guarantee you a good night.

21
00:28:50,967 --> 00:28:52,622
And I'll drop in on here you tomorrow.

22
00:28:52,825 --> 00:28:55,162
Oh, thanks for everything doctor.

23
00:28:56,609 --> 00:29:00,433
- Now, don't worry, I can find my way out.
- I know you can, but do let me help you.

24
00:29:00,596 --> 00:29:04,671
Oh, don't forget that once I'm gone
you'll have to climb those stairs alone.

25
00:29:04,701 --> 00:29:07,867
Oh, I'm all right, I'm armed now.

26
00:29:08,572 --> 00:29:11,739
Can you shoot one of those
things without shutting your eyes?

27
00:29:11,769 --> 00:29:14,703
Oh doctor, there are guns
in every book I've ever written.

28
00:29:14,992 --> 00:29:17,136
I don't write about
things I'm unfamiliar with.

29
00:29:18,497 --> 00:29:19,566
Lock the door Lizzie.

30
00:29:19,596 --> 00:29:21,931
- Good night.
- Yes ma'am, good night doctor.

31
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:26,779
- Accident?
- No, no, the wind blew him down.

32
00:29:26,809 --> 00:29:28,090
- Oh?
- I think.

33
00:29:29,010 --> 00:29:33,521
Did you know that young Mark Fleming leased
you this house without notifying his uncle?

34
00:29:33,850 --> 00:29:35,945
No, no, I didn't.

35
00:29:36,111 --> 00:29:40,046
Well, it doesn't matter now, John
Fleming is dead and Mark is his heir.

36
00:29:40,076 --> 00:29:43,242
But if John were alive, he would warn
you to leave here Miss Van Gorder.

37
00:29:43,272 --> 00:29:44,976
- Really?
- Yes.

38
00:29:45,353 --> 00:29:48,157
It's been a tragic place
for anyone who ever lived in it.

39
00:29:48,338 --> 00:29:50,674
- Well, good night.
- Good night doctor.

40
00:29:51,277 --> 00:29:52,453
Who is out there?

41
00:29:52,831 --> 00:29:55,665
- Nobody you need to worry about doctor.
- Oh, it's Andy.

42
00:29:55,695 --> 00:29:57,627
That's right, good
evening Miss Van Gorder.

43
00:29:57,651 --> 00:29:58,981
Good evening Lieutenant.

44
00:29:59,599 --> 00:30:03,202
- Somebody sick here?
- My maid was bitten by a bat.

45
00:30:03,519 --> 00:30:06,172
Oh? A rabid bat?

46
00:30:06,334 --> 00:30:10,333
Well, I'll know for sure when
I get to my lab, I, I caught the bat.

47
00:30:11,192 --> 00:30:12,700
It happened indoors?

48
00:30:12,730 --> 00:30:14,886
- In my bedroom.
- How it get in?

49
00:30:14,916 --> 00:30:17,238
Well there are ways a
bat could get in a house.

50
00:30:17,901 --> 00:30:19,137
You ought to know.
